# CHANGELOG is append-only: every branch adds entries under the same headings,
# so concurrent PRs collide on the same lines even when the changes are unrelated.
# `merge=union` keeps both sides instead of raising a conflict.
#
# It resolves SILENTLY — ordering can come out odd and nothing flags it — so the
# CHANGELOG still gets eyeballed on every promotion. That is the trade: no false
# conflicts, in exchange for a read.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to apps/*/docs/ASSUMPTIONS_LOG.md. Those are structured
# standards records; a silent union there could interleave two rules into a claim
# neither branch made. Those conflicts are worth resolving by hand.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
